tus is rolled_out and all three regions now report v2.3.0. Next steps: confirm error rate and health checks recover, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2024", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It's the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy in production, and it was the version running in all three regions with a 0.18 error rate.\n- **Rollback status:** Rollout reports `rolled_out`, and all three regions now show v2.3.0. I haven't re-checked health or error rate since the rollback, so that's still to confirm.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback to v2.3.0, and next steps: confirm recovery and investigate v2.3.1 before re-releasing.", "type": "text"}]}]}